title The severity lives in the witness
prompt The baton -- DIFFUSER's lane: moonshots and research, Gauge at Field, hand BAKERY what is buildable. The lap's own cold open named the work before the lane could.
think Lap 4041, rota row 1 -- air, the row that feels. The open read three stashes. Two were the TLB lap already landed; the third, 20260906.070254, held a proven red nobody had landed: signal_trap_scan.sh, signal_trap_control.sh, a REDS row, and two repairs. I checked before believing it -- standing_equipment_run.sh:226 still carried the broken trap and no REDS row named the finding anywhere. Second time this tree nearly lost a whole lap to a stash.
think Reds-first books the allocation, so the lane's own next door waited. What I owed beyond re-landing was the arm the dead lap named and could not run: it wrote "the falsifier is cheap for whoever wants it" and stopped. I am whoever wants it.
think First arm, growth. Running the adopted scan at HEAD read 141 traps against the dead lap's 134, three and a half hours apart. Counting the same predicate at past commits with git grep <rev> gives 119 on 20260831 and 141 ten hours later, and a per-commit walk names 13 commits that each added a site. One of the 13 is this ship's own previous commit, written after the diagnosis was already sitting in this tree's stash. The confound is named rather than hidden: the fleet went three ships to eight across the same window.
think Second arm, consequence. The dead lap proved the mechanism in a pen and said plainly it had not observed a wrong green. A sleep race could not resolve a 300ms fixture, so the signal is triggered on the pen instead -- watch for the fixture's own new /tmp directory and TERM the instant it appears, which puts the signal inside the vulnerable window by construction rather than by luck.
obs THE PREDICTED SEVERE CASE IS REAL AND I WATCHED IT HAPPEN. rye_comment_ascii_control.sh and shell_comment_ascii_control.sh both completed at exit 0 after TERM, publishing files=0 chars=0 where clean reads 4 and 7, every _counted claim flipped yes to no. rye_harness_roster_scan.sh fails the other way at nine signal times -- exit 1, nothing published at all. Which shape a fixture takes turns on where its next write lands, which is an accident of ordering rather than a safety property.
obs AND THE FINDING IS ONE LEVEL UP FROM WHERE THE ROW WAS LOOKING. A fabricated zero is only dangerous if something believes it. ascii_comment_witness.rish asserts on the counts that collapsed, so a signalled control reds loudly -- yet the same witness reads the LIVING scan with exactly two assertions, .ok and under_ceiling=yes, which is the pair a signalled run satisfies falsely. A ceiling claim reads MORE true when the evidence is gone. So the severity is a property of the witness rather than of the script the signal hit, and the population worth counting is believers rather than carriers.
obs I NARROWED THE ROW I WAS ADOPTING RATHER THAN AMPLIFYING IT. The elder text implied 43 fixtures publishing wrong numbers; measured, 43 of 47 are named by a witness, 4 by none, and ZERO by a witness asserting only a verdict-shaped token. The fabrication happens and every witness tested catches it. What stays unresolved is named: whether any witness's asserted tokens ALL survive zeroing, which the static reading cannot decide because under_ceiling=yes is exactly that shape.
obs THE DEAD LAP BUILT A SCAN AND A CONTROL AND ROSTERED NEITHER. Nothing ran either instrument -- the same shape unheard_guard_scan.sh exists to find, arriving before that census could see it. tools/s/signal_trap_witness.rish is written and rostered tier lap at 6s, gating lock_releasing at 0 and reporting files_without_set_e at 47.
obs THE COLD OPEN CAME BACK RED AND IT WAS %440 AGAIN, THE EIGHTH FIRING. A row for 20260906.091519 -- my own last lap's -- stood below 090503 on today's shelf, appended by a rebase rather than inserted. Repaired by hand, which is now the eighth hand-repair of a lantern the card already says is past what a hand should pay. The nib writer closed its twin; this one still has no writer.
obs BOTH PINS WERE FULL AGAIN AND I FOLDED RATHER THAN CUT. REDS stood at 39,658 of 40,960 and my row would not fit, so %470 folded to its own shelf through reds_fold.sh, which re-anchors links the hand forgets -- I had appended the row myself first and had to drop that un-anchored copy, which is %474's lesson arriving in my hands the same hour. The card took the same treatment by hand, links re-anchored one level deeper. Card now 40,952 of 40,960, eight bytes free.
